{"title":"2023 CEMC TUC Problems/Relay B Problem 1","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_CEMC_TUC_Problems/Relay_B_Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Replace <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> below with the number you receive.\n</p><p>At a market, one apple costs <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/8/d/18d8fd61137f32d81435ba367a81cd8c4a9d550e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\$0.50$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"40\" height=\"14\" />, a basket of six apples costs <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/7/c17d72f06af1274f67f7bfd6052714ae79c1e917.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\$2.50$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"40\" height=\"14\" />, and a basket of twelve apples costs <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/8/548449edef6f356497f86f09cf9560103142d19e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\$4.50$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"40\" height=\"14\" />. In dollars, what is the least expensive total price for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/3/f8366cd6196dd8a9da6d38a3e9eafb109e99d53e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> apples?\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_CEMC_TUC_Problems/Relay_B_Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can realize that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> individual apples would cost <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/6/29619b95f4a35909cbb1c0c2f03c0befc2cf272c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\$0.50 \\times 6 = \\$3.00$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"140\" height=\"17\" /> and two baskets of six apples costs <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/d/cfd551aec574545310d4960109eb73d5a3452f3a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\$2.50 \\times 2 = \\$5.00$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"140\" height=\"17\" />. The price of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> individual apples is more than the price of a basket of six and twelve apples from two baskets of six apples costs more than a basket of twelve apples. \n</p><p>This means that we can minimize the price by getting as many baskets of twelve apples as possible, and then as many baskets of six apples as possible.\n</p><p>We can only have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> basket of twelve apples at most because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/c/5/9c5e8086ea82e9ed6f51050766ab2b9e07ca0cbf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12 \\times 1 = 12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"94\" height=\"15\" /> is below <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/3/f8366cd6196dd8a9da6d38a3e9eafb109e99d53e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> but <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/7/227e161fa145426de98336316bc7dc12355b817a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12 \\times 2 = 24$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"94\" height=\"15\" /> is above <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/3/f8366cd6196dd8a9da6d38a3e9eafb109e99d53e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. This means that we should get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> basket of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/f/edf074831eb5bc9e61d6d6e09f525a86e3068f6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> apples, which leaves <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/d/45d82a1582e711a5eae47ce022369ab9c9aa4783.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20 - 12 = 8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"94\" height=\"15\" /> apples remaining.\n</p><p>We can only have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> basket of six apples at most because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/d/e6d7e650ff8a60fd9555b2f0ad3bcc4a90d7fb25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6 \\times 1 = 6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"76\" height=\"15\" /> is below <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/8455f3b5cb3b4880b8c9d782a5c1f0334db819eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> but <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/2/0d2f16950c7b6177e4369d317ee7857b5314c853.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6 \\times 2 = 12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"85\" height=\"15\" /> is above <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/8455f3b5cb3b4880b8c9d782a5c1f0334db819eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. This means that we should get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> basket of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> apples, which leaves <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/d/33da4a95c7f1a2454ec964589807b362bc55d4fa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8 - 6 = 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"76\" height=\"15\" /> apples remaining. We would then have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> individual apples.\n</p><p>The total price would be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/0/870d90edf8700d559929b847da6cb07c84842ee7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\$4.50 \\times 1 + \\$2.50 \\times 1 + \\$0.50 \\times 2 = \\$4.50 + \\$2.50 + \\$1.00$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"457\" height=\"17\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/4/1b44805f0cb35bc7a82dfbbfd6060dcfa1e5876d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\$7.00 + \\$1.00 = \\boxed{\\$8.00}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -7px\" width=\"184\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_CEMC_TUC\" title=\"2023 CEMC TUC\">2023 CEMC TUC</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_CEMC_TUC_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2023 CEMC TUC Problems (page does not exist)\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_CEMC_TUC_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2023 CEMC TUC Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_CEMC_TUC_Problems/Relay_A_Problem_4\" title=\"2023 CEMC TUC Problems/Relay A Problem 4\">Relay A Problem 4</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_CEMC_TUC_Problems/Relay_B_Problem_2\" title=\"2023 CEMC TUC Problems/Relay B Problem 2\">Relay B Problem 2</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_CEMC_TUC_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2023 CEMC TUC Problems/Problem 1 (page does not exist)\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_CEMC_TUC_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2023 CEMC TUC Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_CEMC_TUC_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2023 CEMC TUC Problems/Problem 3 (page does not exist)\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_CEMC_TUC_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2023 CEMC TUC Problems/Problem 4 (page does not exist)\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_CEMC_TUC_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2023 CEMC TUC Problems/Problem 5 (page does not exist)\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_CEMC_TUC_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2023 CEMC TUC Problems/Problem 6 (page does not exist)\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_CEMC_TUC_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2023 CEMC TUC Problems/Problem 7 (page does not exist)\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_CEMC_TUC_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2023 CEMC TUC Problems/Problem 8 (page does not exist)\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_CEMC_TUC_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2023 CEMC TUC Problems/Problem 9 (page does not exist)\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_CEMC_TUC_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2023 CEMC TUC Problems/Problem 10 (page does not exist)\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_CEMC_TUC_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2023 CEMC TUC Problems/Problem 11 (page does not exist)\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_CEMC_TUC_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2023 CEMC TUC Problems/Problem 12 (page does not exist)\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_CEMC_TUC_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2023 CEMC TUC Problems/Problem 13 (page does not exist)\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_CEMC_TUC_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2023 CEMC TUC Problems/Problem 14 (page does not exist)\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_CEMC_TUC_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2023 CEMC TUC Problems/Problem 15 (page does not exist)\">15</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_CEMC_TUC_Problems/Crossnumber_Puzzle&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2023 CEMC TUC Problems/Crossnumber Puzzle (page does not exist)\">Crossnumber Puzzle</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_CEMC_TUC_Problems/Logic_Puzzle&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2023 CEMC TUC Problems/Logic Puzzle (page do